  = must: invalidate this canonical record when the source hash changes without reprocessing

& [CanonicalRequirementSet: AlienHandCodexStreamWorker] is the stable requirement set
  + [requirement] is AlienHand runtime emits durable request events instead of depending on blocking Codex calls
  + [requirement] is SQLite is the prototype control-plane store for requests, responses, attempts, leases, and artifacts
  + [requirement] is every request has request_id, app_id, task_type, input_ref, created_at, and replayable evidence
  + [requirement] is every final response references one request_id and records status, result_ref or error_ref, model route, and artifact or justification references where available
  + [requirement] is worker execution uses claim leases, heartbeat, retry, poison handling, idempotency, and graceful shutdown
  + [requirement] is task routing distinguishes SOP compile, route decision, LLM decision, history context pack, spec explosion, justification record, tool handoff, and health check
  + [requirement] is model selection records Spark-suitable versus high-reasoning decisions under Model_Budget_Routing
  + [requirement] is response artifacts are written before successful completion status when the response depends on them
  + [requirement] is failures are durable and replayable rather than console-only
  + [requirement] is ordinary chat-sourced requests cannot trigger arbitrary shell, filesystem, network, or repo mutations without trusted task authorization

  = must: treat these requirements as implementation blockers for the first prototype
  = must: preserve implementation deviations in solution or justification records

& [CanonicalImplementationFrontier: AlienHandCodexStreamWorker] is the ordered work frontier
  + [frontier_1] is create SQLite control-plane schema for requests, responses, attempts, leases, and artifacts
  + [frontier_2] is add Python service APIs for enqueue, claim, heartbeat, complete, fail, cancel, and status
  + [frontier_3] is add a worker loop with pluggable fake executor and graceful shutdown
  + [frontier_4] is add task routing module that records Spark-suitable versus high-reasoning choices
  + [frontier_5] is add SOP task executor stubs for compile, spec_explosion, justification_record, route_decision, and health_check
  + [frontier_6] is integrate AlienHand runtime or chat commands with durable request creation
  + [frontier_7] is add UI/debug visibility for pending/completed/failed worker requests
  + [frontier_8] is add production authentication, retention, and multi-worker policy after prototype proof

  = must: complete frontier_1 through frontier_3 before relying on live model-backed task execution
  = must: use fake executor tests to prove queue lifecycle before paid or interactive LLM calls
  = must: record coherent completed slices as justification evidence

& [Justification: AlienHandCodexStreamWorker] is the evidence bridge for accepting this canonical specification
  + [claim] is the stream-worker subject is ready for bounded prototype implementation
  + [support] is preserved source seed, source hash, seven-fold trace, explicit control-plane boundary, request and response contracts, worker lifecycle, model routing contract, failure policy, and implementation frontier
  + [confidence] is high for prototype architecture, local durability model, worker lifecycle shape, replay posture, and model-budget routing boundary
  + [confidence] is moderate for production authentication, long-running unattended Codex execution, retention policy, and distributed queue selection because those remain intentionally deferred
  + [counterargument] is Codex itself may not be the only runtime implementation of the worker; the contract should allow later worker executors without changing AlienHand request and response events
  + [invalidation_condition] is source_change, failed_queue_lifecycle_proof, unsafe_task_authorization, broken_artifact_ordering, model_route_policy_conflict, or implementation_contradiction

  ! [CodexStreamWorkerSpecAcceptedForPrototype] is accepted
    @ [support] [CanonicalRequirementSet: AlienHandCodexStreamWorker]
    @ [support] [CanonicalImplementationFrontier: AlienHandCodexStreamWorker]
    @ [support] [SatisfactionSignature: AlienHandCodexStreamWorker]

& [SolutionTrackingSeed: AlienHandCodexStreamWorker] is the initial solution tracking state
  + [implemented] is source seed preservation, exploded specification, canonical record, seven-fold trace, requirement set, and implementation frontier
  + [not_yet_implemented] is SQLite control-plane schema, service API, worker loop, task routing module, SOP executor stubs, AlienHand integration, debug UI visibility, and production auth or retention policy
  + [next_valid_work] is [CanonicalImplementationFrontier: AlienHandCodexStreamWorker] frontier_1

  = must: update solution or justification records when frontier items are implemented
  = must: distinguish implemented specification artifacts from unimplemented runtime behavior

